<title>EGYPT: Egyptian crude, natgas production rose in October.</title>
<headline>Egyptian crude, natgas production rose in October.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian crude oil production was up to an average 830,000 barrels per day (bpd) in October from 827,000 bpd in September, the state's Egyptian General Petroleum Corporation (EGPC) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Natural gas output also rose to 1.32 billion cubic feet a day from 1.307 in September.</p>
<p>Condensate production fell to 36,000 bpd from 36,700 bpd while propane and butane output rose to 32,000 bpd from 31,000 bpd, it said.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +2 02 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
